note.text:
Applications: health (reading scans, spotting disease), agriculture (identifying crop diseases from phone photos, forecasting weather), education (tutoring apps), transport (route planning), business (answering customers), security (detecting fraud) and accessibility (reading text aloud for blind people).
Ethical problems:
• bias: AI trained on unfair or one-sided data can treat some people unfairly;
• privacy: AI uses personal data that must be protected;
• misinformation: AI can produce false text and fake images or videos (deepfakes);
• jobs: some tasks are automated;
• over-reliance: people may stop thinking or checking.
Responsible use: check facts with other sources, do not share personal data, say honestly when you used AI, and do not use it to cheat or to harm others.
